<h2>How the calculation works</h2><p>Prorated earned salary = eligible monthly salary ÷ salary-day divisor × payable days. Gross settlement adds leave encashment and other payable additions. Net estimate subtracts notice-period recovery and other entered deductions.</p><h2>How to use the result</h2><p>Use the calculator as a reconciliation worksheet after HR/payroll has identified the actual payable and recoverable components. Keeping notice recovery as a separate input makes the settlement logic visible.</p><h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2><p>Final settlement can also include bonus, incentives, gratuity, reimbursements, asset recovery, loans, statutory deductions and tax. Notice-pay rights and salary proration rules depend on contracts, policies and law. The tool does not determine what may legally be deducted.</p><h2>Example</h2><p>Review each input against the employee's final payslip calculation rather than treating the result as an automatic payroll instruction.</p>
